    </p>
    <p class="authors">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Authors:</span>
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Reddy%2C+T+R">Tella Rajashekhar Reddy</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Deshmukh%2C+A">Atharva Deshmukh</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Tandon%2C+K">Karan Tandon</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Gandhi%2C+R">Rohan Gandhi</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Parayil%2C+A">Anjaly Parayil</a>, 
      
      <a href="/search/?searchtype=author&amp;query=Bhattacherjee%2C+D">Debopam Bhattacherjee</a>
      
    </p>
    
    <p class="abstract mathjax">
      <span class="has-text-black-bis has-text-weight-semibold">Abstract</span>:
      <span class="abstract-short has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.15330v1-abstract-short" style="display: inline;">
        Large language <span class="search-hit mathjax">model</span> (&hellip;
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.15330v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'inline'; document.getElementById('2510.15330v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'none';">&#9661; More</a>
      </span>
      <span class="abstract-full has-text-grey-dark mathjax" id="2510.15330v1-abstract-full" style="display: none;">
        Large language <span class="search-hit mathjax">model</span> (<span class="search-hit mathjax">LLM</span>) applications are blindfolded to the infrastructure underneath and generate tokens autoregressively, indifferent to the system load, thus risking inferencing latency inflation and poor user experience. Our first-cut controller, named beLLMan, enables the <span class="search-hit mathjax">LLM</span> infrastructure to actively and progressively signal the first-party <span class="search-hit mathjax">LLM</span> application to adjust the output length in response to changing system load. On a real testbed with H100 <span class="search-hit mathjax">GPUs</span>, beLLMan helps keep inferencing latency under control (upto 8X lower end-to-end latency) and reduces energy consumption by 25% (while <span class="search-hit mathjax">serving</span> 19% more requests) during periods of congestion for a summarization workload.
        <a class="is-size-7" style="white-space: nowrap;" onclick="document.getElementById('2510.15330v1-abstract-full').style.display = 'none'; document.getElementById('2510.15330v1-abstract-short').style.display = 'inline';">&#9651; Less</a>
      </span>
    </p>
    

